/*
  RangeSlider.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0224 · RangeSlider (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web `components/ui/RangeSlider.tsx` resolves
  two keys for the per-thumb accessible names — `slider.thumbMin` ("{{label}} minimum") and `slider.thumbMax`
  ("{{label}} maximum") — both mirrored verbatim below (the `{{label}}` placeholder is interpolated at
  runtime with the caller's already-localized `label`). The remaining entries are native a11y / HIG
  additions: the spoken range connector (the visible row uses an en-dash, which VoiceOver should not read
  literally) and the degenerate-range affordance copy (the "never a blank box" peer of a `max <= min`
  slider with nothing to adjust).

  These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept
  in a per-surface table ("RangeSlider") so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings. In test /
  preview bundles `NSLocalizedString` returns the value below, keeping the labels deterministic.
*/

/* --- Web t() keys mirrored from components/ui/RangeSlider.tsx --- */

/* Accessible name for the low thumb (web slider.thumbMin); {{label}} = the range's label. */
"slider.thumbMin" = "{{label}} minimum";

/* Accessible name for the high thumb (web slider.thumbMax); {{label}} = the range's label. */
"slider.thumbMax" = "{{label}} maximum";

/* --- Native a11y / HIG additions (no web t() key) --- */

/* Spoken connector between the low and high values in the label row's summary, e.g. "0 to 100". */
"slider.rangeConnector" = "to";

/* Title of the degenerate-range affordance, shown when max <= min (nothing to adjust). */
"slider.empty" = "No range to adjust";

/* Supporting line of the degenerate-range affordance. */
"slider.emptyMessage" = "A range appears here once the minimum and maximum differ.";
